    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0602" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.24/99</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of Controls</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Green</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-18">November 18, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Green</hi>: The Greek Minister called to see me
                    to take up the matter mentioned in your memorandum.<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d504-f1"/> I told him I would try to give him a definite reply by
                    Wednesday afternoon. In other words, I see no reason for letting the Greek
                    Government continue to have the hope of our doing something if it cannot be
                    done. The question is one of vital importance to them as I understand it. I
                    shall talk with General Marshall and the Secretary of War personally about this
                    and let you know.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
